  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef decided to exercise by running somewhere from ShareChat. He chose three sets of points in a plane:\n\n\nA set of NNN points (numbered 111 through NNN): for each valid iii, the iii-th of them has coordinates (ai,bi)(a_i, b_i)(ai​,bi​).\nA set of MMM points (numbered 111 through MMM): for each valid iii, the iii-th of them has coordinates (ci,di)(c_i, d_i)(ci​,di​).\nA set of KKK points (numbered 111 through KKK): for each valid iii, the iii-th of them has coordinates (ei,fi)(e_i, f_i)(ei​,fi​).\nShareChat has coordinates (x,y)(x, y)(x,y). Chef must choose one point (aj,bj)(a_j, b_j)(aj​,bj​), one point (ck,dk)(c_k, d_k)(ck​,dk​), and one point (el,fl)(e_l, f_l)(el​,fl​). Then, he starts running from ShareChat, visits the chosen points (aj,bj)(a_j, b_j)(aj​,bj​) and (ck,dk)(c_k, d_k)(ck​,dk​) in any order, and then runs to the point (el,fl)(e_l, f_l)(el​,fl​), where he finishes his run.\n\nHelp Chef find the minimum distance he has to run.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤5,0001 \\le T \\le 5,0001≤T≤5,000",
      "1≤N,M,K≤5,0001 \\le N, M, K \\le 5,0001≤N,M,K≤5,000",
      "0≤x,y≤1090 \\le x, y \\le 10^90≤x,y≤109",
      "0≤ai,bi≤1090 \\le a_i, b_i \\le 10^90≤ai​,bi​≤109 for each valid iii",
      "0≤ci,di≤1090 \\le c_i, d_i \\le 10^90≤ci​,di​≤109 for each valid iii",
      "0≤ei,fi≤1090 \\le e_i, f_i \\le 10^90≤ei​,fi​≤109 for each valid iii",
      "the sum of N+M+KN+M+KN+M+K over all test cases does not exceed 15,00015,00015,000",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (50 points):** 1≤N,M,K≤1001 \\le N, M, K \\le 1001≤N,M,K≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers xxx and yyy.\nThe second line contains three space-separated integers NNN, MMM and KKK.\nThe third line contains 2N2N2N space-separated integers a1,b1,a2,b2,…,aN,bNa_1, b_1, a_2, b_2, \\ldots, a_N, b_Na1​,b1​,a2​,b2​,…,aN​,bN​.\nThe fourth line contains 2M2M2M space-separated integers c1,d1,c2,d2,…,cM,dMc_1, d_1, c_2, d_2, \\ldots, c_M, d_Mc1​,d1​,c2​,d2​,…,cM​,dM​.\nThe fifth line contains 2K2K2K space-separated integers e1,f1,e2,f2,…,eK,fKe_1, f_1, e_2, f_2, \\ldots, e_K, f_Ke1​,f1​,e2​,f2​,…,eK​,fK​.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing one real number ― the minimum distance.\n\nYour answer will be considered correct if its absolute or relative error does not exceed 10−610^{-6}10−6.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
